     9	Provides 2D sprite and mesh rendering for Bevy.
    10	
    11	## 2D Lighting
    12	
    13	The sprite renderer includes forward-rendered 2D lighting that works with the
    14	existing sprite and `Mesh2d` pipelines:
    15	
    16	- Add a `normal_map` to a `Sprite`, or a `normal_map` to a `ColorMaterial`, to
    17	  shade surface detail. Normal maps should use a linear texture format.
    18	- Add any number of `PointLight2d` components, up to `MAX_LIGHTS_2D` per view.
    19	- Add `LightOccluder2d` polygons or polylines to cast dynamic shadows.
    20	- Configure global light with the `AmbientLight2d` resource. Its default is
    21	  white at full brightness, so scenes without point lights look unchanged.
    22	
    23	Sprite lighting is enabled by `SpriteRenderPlugin`; no extra camera or render
    24	pass is required. Custom `Material2d` shaders can import the shared lighting
    25	functions from `package::light2d::lighting`.
    26	
    27	See the [`lighting_2d`](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/main/examples/2d/lighting_2d.rs)
    28	example for a complete scene.

